  built-in pool; sa_reks_weights defaults to a uniform average; sa_reks_extra
  adds raw determinants [alpha(M)|beta(M)] to the SA ensemble only.

  Bulk tokens (in place of indices/names): 'full' selects the whole manifold
  config block; a config type ('PPS', 'OSS', ...) selects every config of that
  type, e.g. si_reks_configs [['full']] or [['PPS', 'OSS']].
  'single-scheme:N' selects the configs of pairing scheme N and 'mixed-scheme:N'
  the SSR state set on scheme N (open-shell singlets from every scheme); the
  spin-projected configs are the base and ride along with either. Both default to 0
  and take several indices ('single-scheme-1-2-3' unions the three) or scheme
  classes relative to scheme 0: 'T' (one transposition of antibonding partners),
  'D<k>' (k disjoint transpositions), 'C<l>' (an l-cycle), e.g.
